- **Literal names.** Duplicating "Aggro (copy)" gives "Aggro (copy) (copy)", following the issue's `<name> (copy)` exactly. Rejected: stripping a trailing "(copy n)" first, which would mean parsing a localised suffix.
- **The name is cut to fit.** The original's name is shortened so the suffix survives the 40-character cap. Rejected: letting the save's cut drop " (copy)", which would repeat the original's name.
- **List action shape.** A per-row icon button whose accessible name and tooltip are "Duplicate {deck}". Rejected: a worded per-row button (wraps the narrow rail) and a group-head button acting on the open deck (on a phone it is unclear which deck it copies).
- **Editor reason.** The editor states its own reason at the cap, because a phone's editor half hides the rail's note.
- **Save timing.** The copy saves through the usual debounce, not at once.

